  "id": "Compound::DB00703 - Gene::763",
  "verbalization": "Methazolamide is linked to Ca5a through a series of molecular interactions that involve carbonic anhydrase inhibition and hydration processes. The evidence suggests that Methazolamide binds to Ca6 or Ca12, which in turn participate in reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. This process is ultimately linked to Ca5a, indicating a potential role in the regulation of carbon dioxide levels. The presence of a common ancestor, Organic Heterocyclic Compound, further supports a shared biochemical pathway. The relationship between Methazolamide and Ca5a is thus mediated through the carbonic anhydrase inhibition and hydration mechanisms, highlighting a functional connection in the context of cellular metabolic processes.",
